# Assignment 2 — Personal Mission Statement

## Personal Mission
My goal is to use computer science and cybersecurity to make technology safer and more trustworthy for the people who depend on it. I want to develop strong technical skills, take responsibility for my work, and help people protect their information. I am especially interested in security for government or cloud systems, where reliability, privacy, and ethical decisions are important.

## Short-term goals (1–3 years)
While studying Computer Science at the University of South Carolina, I want to build a solid foundation in programming, networking, operating systems, and information security. I plan to participate in cybersecurity activities, practice hands-on challenges, improve my GitHub portfolio, and apply for internships or research opportunities.

**Success criteria:** Complete my foundational coursework, publish at least three carefully documented projects, participate regularly in cybersecurity activities, and apply for relevant internships.

## Medium-term goals (4–7 years)
I want to graduate with a Computer Science degree and begin a position such as security analyst, cloud security engineer, or security engineer. I would like to gain experience responding to security problems, reviewing systems for weaknesses, and designing practical defenses. I will keep learning about networking, cloud infrastructure, and secure software development.

**Success criteria:** Graduate, secure an entry-level cybersecurity role, contribute to at least one deployed security improvement, and build a record of responsible professional work.

## Long-term goals (8+ years)
I hope to grow into a cybersecurity specialist or technical leader who helps organizations protect sensitive systems. I want to mentor students interested in technology, especially students who have not had easy access to computing opportunities. I also want to maintain a healthy balance between career growth, family, and community commitments.

**Success criteria:** Lead or substantially contribute to a security program, mentor newer professionals or students, and maintain a sustainable life outside work.

## Organizations and roles that interest me
- Roles: cybersecurity analyst, incident responder, security engineer, cloud security engineer.
- Organizations: U.S. government cybersecurity agencies, public-sector contractors, cloud service providers, and universities conducting cybersecurity research. These are **interests**, not job offers.

## How my major and courses support these goals
Computer Science builds the programming and problem-solving skills needed for secure systems. Data structures and algorithms will help me write and analyze efficient code. Networking, operating systems, and security electives will help me understand how computers communicate, where vulnerabilities occur, and how defenses work. Ethics coursework is important because security decisions affect users' privacy and trust.

## How the stages fit together
The technical knowledge, teamwork, and portfolio I develop during college will help me earn internships and an entry-level role. Those experiences will allow me to grow toward senior responsibilities and ultimately use what I learn to improve security and support others.

